{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Justified feels like a natural next choice because its crime stories, tense confrontations, and sharp dialogue connect with what I enjoy in True Romance and 24.",
    "The Man in the High Castle appeals to my interest in suspense and political intrigue, even though Justified fits my current mood more closely."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Good Wife's legal drama is less appealing right now because I want crime and action suspense rather than courtroom conflict.",
    "I cannot judge the untitled items without knowing their stories; I passed on them because their fit is uncertain, not because I know I would dislike them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Sharing dramatic tension is not enough to make a legal drama as appealing to me as a tense crime story.",
    "Popularity alone gives me no reason to choose an unidentified item; I need a connection to the kind of story I want."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent interaction with 24 makes immediate danger and sustained suspense especially relevant to what I want now.",
    "The combination of crime, tense confrontations, and sharp dialogue matters more to my choice than a broad resemblance to other dramas."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly captured my interest in suspense, but Justified best matches the crime, action, and dialogue I want right now."
}"}
